Both `cargo check` and `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` pass clean.

**Summary:** One change applied — removed the module-level `#![allow(non_camel_case_types)]` from `picoquic_logger.rs`. This module defines no types (no `struct`, `enum`, `type alias`, or `trait`), so the allow was dead lint suppression that would mislead a reader into expecting a C-style type alias somewhere in the file. All other aspects of the translation were already correct: `picoquic_connection_id_t` is `Copy` so pass-by-value is right, `Option<&str>` correctly captures the NULL-as-stop-sentinel C contract, `&mut dyn core::fmt::Write` is a sound `FILE*` replacement for `no_std` compatibility, `&[u8]` correctly collapses the `(uint8_t*, uint16_t)` pair, and `#[allow(clippy::result_unit_err)]` is properly scoped to just the single `Result<(),()>` function.


